{
  "reasoning": "Incorrect. The Customs Declaration, Assessment and Re-assessment Rules, 2024 expressly allow and require electronic submission and payment. For example, Document 1 (_clause 3_) states that all documents referred to in rule 4 shall be accepted electronically. Document 6 (_clause 7(1)_) provides that a document or payment effected electronically in a Customs computer system shall be deemed properly submitted. Document 9 (_clause 4_) provides for applicants to seek permission from the Commissioner to submit documents electronically, and Document 3 (Customs Act s.79A) contemplates acceptance of electronically transmitted bills of entry. While Document 6 (_clause 7(2)_) allows the Commissioner in special circumstances to require signed paper copies, that is an exception — not support for the claim that only physical paper documents are accepted. Therefore the statement that only physical paper-based documents are accepted is factually inaccurate.",
  "verdict": "INCORRECT"
}

